  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🖤 Emo Band Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Long sentence names, Midwest emo and pop-emo, all in one place."
    },
    "intro": "Good emo band names come in two sizes: a few plain words about the suburbs, like Bike Rack Kids, or a whole sentence about your feelings, like Everyone I Know Is Doing Fine, Thanks. This **emo band name generator** does both, with Midwest emo, long sentence-style names and 2000s pop-emo, plus solo artist names and album titles.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good emo band names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Everyone I Know Is Doing Fine, Thanks</strong>: a sentence name with a sting at the end.</li><li><strong>Our Old House Wants to Talk</strong>: nostalgia for a place, which is half of emo.</li><li><strong>I Moved Out in October</strong>: a date and a life change.</li><li><strong>Bike Rack Kids</strong>: Midwest emo's small, suburban details.</li><li><strong>Corn Maze Society</strong>: a club named after a very specific autumn memory.</li><li><strong>Spelling Bee Ghosts</strong>: school days, turned sad.</li><li><strong>Dad's Old Car</strong>: a solo-project name that sounds like a song.</li><li><strong>All My Friends Are Moving to Chicago</strong>: an album title that tells a whole story.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where emo names come from",
        "content": "<p>Emo began in Washington, DC in the mid-1980s as \"emotional hardcore\", with bands like Rites of Spring and Embrace. It grew in three waves, and each one named itself differently:</p><ul><li><strong>Midwest emo</strong> in the 1990s: twinkly guitars and small-town memories. American Football's first album, in 1999, put a house in Urbana, Illinois on the cover, and the house became as famous as the band. Names here are like that: <em>Hall Pass Season</em>, <em>Paper Drive</em>.</li><li><strong>Long sentence names</strong>, a tradition of the 2010s revival. The best-known is The World Is a Beautiful Place &amp; I Am No Longer Afraid to Die. Here: <em>My Heart Is a Snow Day</em>.</li><li><strong>2000s pop-emo</strong>, when the scene went mainstream with bands like My Chemical Romance and Fall Out Boy, whose song titles were famously long. Names here: <em>Postcard Avenue</em>, <em>Letters for Lost Friends</em>.</li></ul><p>Choose <strong>Solo artist</strong> for a real-sounding name like <em>Jenna Walczak</em> or a project like <em>Night Swimmer</em>, and <strong>Album title</strong> for records like <em>You Can Keep the Hoodie</em>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using an emo name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Long names get shortened.</strong> Fans will turn a sentence into initials, so check those too.</li><li><strong>Specific beats general.</strong> \"Corn maze\" and \"bike rack\" say more than \"sadness\".</li><li><strong>Search before you commit.</strong> Look the name up on Spotify, Bandcamp and YouTube, and check the social handles are free. Two acts with one name confuse fans and streaming services alike.</li></ul><p>For the louder, catchier side of the scene, try the <a href=\"pop-punk-band-name-generator.html\">Pop Punk Band Name Generator</a>, and for something slower and quieter, the <a href=\"slowcore-band-name-generator.html\">Slowcore Band Name Generator</a>. The <a href=\"song-title-generator.html\">Song Title Generator</a> is good at the long, confessional titles emo loves, and the <a href=\"band-name-generator.html\">Band Name Generator</a> covers every genre.</p><p>For more genres, see all the <a href=\"../categories/music_genres-names.html\">music genre name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good emo band names?",
        "answer": "Either a short, specific memory, like Bike Rack Kids or Corn Maze Society, or a whole sentence, like Our Old House Wants to Talk. Both work; it depends whether your band is Midwest emo or the long-name kind."
